        "original_id": "5bc5bb90-d3ff-5c7d-a7ef-04c99cbeb2ee",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tahmoh Penikett, Joss Whedon\n- Characters: Karl C. Agathon\n- Organizations: Mutant Enemy Productions, Bellwether Pictures\n- TV series: Supernatural, Dollhouse, Continuum, Buffy the Vampire Slayer, Angel, Firefly, Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D., Battlestar Galactica\n\nFacts:\n- Joss Whedon founded Mutant Enemy Productions and co-founded Bellwether Pictures.\n- Joss Whedon created the television series Buffy the Vampire Slayer (1997–2003), Angel (1999–2004), Firefly (2002), Dollhouse (2009–10), and Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. (from 2013).\n- Tahmoh Penikett starred in the TV series Supernatural, Joss Whedon’s Dollhouse, and the Showtime time travel show Continuum.\n- Karl C. Agathon, callsign Helo, is a fictional character on the re-imagined Battlestar Galactica TV series.\n- Tahmoh Penikett portrayed Karl C. Agathon on the re-imagined Battlestar Galactica TV series.",
